---
import { site } from "../../data/site";
import RollDie from "./faq/RollDie.astro";
---

<section class="section faq" id="faq">
    <div class="sec-head">
        <div class="sec-rail">
            <p class="kicker">Sec. 07 / Troubleshooting</p>
            <p class="fig-label">FIG. 09 — Q &amp; A</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sec-body">
            <h2>The fine print.</h2>
            <p class="lead">
                The store, the hardware, the permissions, the network —
                the answers we give most often, in full,{" "}
                <em>license terms included.</em>
            </p>
            <RollDie />
        </div>
    </div>

    <details>
        <summary>Is it on the Play Store?</summary>
        <p>
            Not yet. The alpha ships as a signed APK you install
            yourself. The full build can drive other apps through
            Android accessibility, which Play restricts — a reduced
            build is planned for stores, while the full one stays
            sideloaded.
        </p>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>Why a starter build and then a full build?</summary>
        <p>
            Play Protect blocks any app downloaded through a browser,
            messaging app or file manager that declares an accessibility
            service (“App blocked to protect your device”, no install
            anyway). The full build declares one; the starter build does
            not, so it installs. The starter build then downloads the
            full build and hands it to Android's installer, which Play
            Protect allows. Both are signed with the same key, so your
            data is kept.
        </p>
        <p>
            “App blocked to protect your device” on the starter build, or
            “App not installed”? Uninstall any older or debug PhoneCanDo
            build first (different signing key), and check the APK is
            {site.size}, {site.arch} and matches the SHA-256 above. With a
            computer, <code>adb install</code> of the full APK skips the
            block entirely.
        </p>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>The accessibility toggle says “denied access”.</summary>
        <p>
            Android 13+ locks that toggle for apps installed outside a
            store. PhoneCanDo walks you through it in Settings → Phone
            control: Android shows its “Restricted setting” note (tap OK),
            then App info → ⋮ (top right) → <strong>Allow restricted
            settings</strong>, then the toggle. The ⋮ item only appears
            after that note, so do the steps in order.
        </p>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>Do I need a computer?</summary>
        <p>
            No. Setup, the agent, the terminal and the model keys
            all live on the phone.
        </p>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>Which phones does it run on?</summary>
        <p>
            Arm64 devices on Android {site.minAndroid} or newer,
            with 2 GB free. It will not run on x86 emulators or
            32-bit phones.
        </p>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>What can it actually control?</summary>
        <p>
            Any app with a visible UI: tapping, typing, scrolling,
            reading the screen, plus notifications, clipboard,
            sharing and intents. Actions that change the phone need
            a biometric unlock first.
        </p>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>Does it need a constant connection?</summary>
        <p>
            The agent and your files run locally. Model calls go to
            the provider you configure, so it needs network for
            those — unless you point it at a local endpoint. The
            update check and the usage stats use the network too,
            but nothing waits for them.
        </p>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>Does it send anything about me?</summary>
        <p>
            Anonymous usage stats, on by default: phone model, Android
            and app version, which features get used, crashes and
            engine errors. Never your prompts, sessions, files, keys or
            screen. One switch in Settings → Privacy turns it off, and
            Delete my data erases what the server holds for your phone.
            Every field is listed in the{" "}
            <a href="/privacy/">privacy note</a>.
        </p>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>Can I use the source?</summary>
        <p>
            The source is on{" "}
            <a href={site.repo} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                GitHub
            </a>{" "}
            under a source-available license. You can read it and
            contribute; you cannot copy, use, or redistribute it.
            The official app is the only distributed build.
        </p>
    </details>
    <details>
        <summary>How do I reach you?</summary>
        <p>
            Bugs and feature requests: open an{" "}
            <a href={`${site.repo}/issues`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                issue on GitHub
            </a>, so others can find the answer too. Help with your
            install or your data:{" "}
            <a href={`mailto:${site.email.support}`}>{site.email.support}</a>.
            Anything else:{" "}
            <a href={`mailto:${site.email.hi}`}>{site.email.hi}</a>.
        </p>
    </details>
</section>

<style is:global>
    .faq details { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .faq details:first-of-type { border-top: 0; }
    .faq summary {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
      padding: 16px 0;
      cursor: pointer;
      list-style: none;
      font: 500 15px/1.45 var(--sans);
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }
    .faq summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
    .faq summary::before {
      content: 'Q.';
      font: 500 9px/1 var(--mono);
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      color: var(--accent-ink);
    }
    .faq summary:hover::before { animation: faq-q 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1); }
    /* Open, the plus spins round into a red cross. */
    .faq summary::after {
      content: '+';
      margin-left: auto;
      font: 400 15px/1 var(--mono);
      color: var(--faint);
      transition: rotate 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1), color 0.2s;
    }
    .faq summary:hover::after { color: var(--fg); }
    .faq details[open] summary::after { rotate: 135deg; color: var(--red); }
    .faq details[open] p { animation: faq-open 0.3s ease-out; }
    /* The question the die picked flashes amber. */
    .faq details[data-rolled] summary { animation: faq-rolled 1.2s ease-out; }
    .faq details[data-rolled] summary::before { color: var(--red); }
    .faq details p {
      position: relative;
      padding: 0 0 18px 26px;
      max-width: 78ch;
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    .faq details p::before {
      content: 'A.';
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      top: 1px;
      font: 500 9px/1 var(--mono);
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      color: var(--red);
    }
    .faq details p code { font: 400 12.5px var(--mono); color: var(--fg); }
    .faq details p a { color: var(--fg); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-2); }
    .faq details p a:hover { color: var(--red); border-bottom-color: var(--red); }

    @keyframes faq-q { 50% { translate: 0 -4px; } }
    @keyframes faq-open { from { opacity: 0; translate: 0 -6px; } }
    @keyframes faq-rolled {
      from { background-color: var(--accent-soft); box-shadow: 0 0 0 10px var(--accent-soft); }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .faq summary::after { transition: none; }
      .faq summary:hover::before,
      .faq details[open] p,
      .faq details[data-rolled] summary { animation: none; }
    }
</style>
